WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.867
(audience cheers)

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.464
- Hello, nice to meet you.

00:00:02.464 --> 00:00:03.297
Have y'all ever met?

00:00:03.297 --> 00:00:04.130
Have you ever met Ana?

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.130
- No, it's our first time.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:05.963
- Hi.

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:06.990
- [Kelly] Hello.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:07.823
- [Phil] How's it going for you so far?

00:00:07.823 --> 00:00:08.656
- Oh, so far it's going great.

00:00:08.656 --> 00:00:09.489
- [Phil] Great.

00:00:09.489 --> 00:00:10.322
- [Ana] Yes.
- [Phil] Good.

00:00:10.322 --> 00:00:11.155
(all laugh)

00:00:11.155 --> 00:00:13.140
- So you, and the Ted Lasso cast just went

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.070
to the White House.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.000
Had you ever been there before?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.050
Did you like it?

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.010
- Oh no.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:17.843
It was fine.

00:00:17.843 --> 00:00:18.676
- [Ana] It was cool?

00:00:18.676 --> 00:00:19.509
- [Phil] Yeah.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:20.342
(audience laughs and claps)

00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:21.175
- [Phil] No, it was...

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:22.008
- [Kelly] I just love this photo.

00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:22.920
That's a boss photo.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.120
- [Phil] I don't know, man, I mean.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.050
- Did you get a tour?

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.302
- We did get a tour, yeah.

00:00:26.302 --> 00:00:27.135
- Okay.

00:00:27.135 --> 00:00:27.968
- It's so funny, it's so silly.

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:28.801
Look at us all there.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:29.634
Like, what are we doing there?

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.674
- Silly?
I think you look very cool.

00:00:31.674 --> 00:00:32.507
- Thanks, man.

00:00:32.507 --> 00:00:36.390
Yeah, no, it was a
total riot and also wild

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.488
because I don't know,
you see the Oval Office

00:00:39.488 --> 00:00:42.120
so often in like TV shows and films.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.820
You're like, "Is it real? Is this real?"

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.653
When you're in there, you're like,

00:00:45.653 --> 00:00:46.868
"This is the real one, right?"

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:48.660
- No, I've been in it and it's crazy.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.830
You feel, yeah, like you're in ...

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.725
- [Phil] The whole thing was surreal.

00:00:50.725 --> 00:00:51.558
- ... the West Wing.
- [Phil] Yeah.

00:00:51.558 --> 00:00:52.391
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:52.391 --> 00:00:55.351
So in the show we get, Ted brings ...

00:00:55.351 --> 00:00:56.184
- [Kelly] Biscuits.

00:00:56.184 --> 00:00:57.180
- The biscuits.
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.970
- And they very kindly gave us this

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.410
little box of biscuits with

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.953
a president of the
United States seal on it.

00:01:02.953 --> 00:01:04.200
- Oh, that's cool.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.610
- That's cute.
- Very cool.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:09.145
I was like, "Can I have another
one for my dad, please?"

00:01:09.145 --> 00:01:09.978
(audience laughs)

00:01:09.978 --> 00:01:10.811
- That's thoughtful.

00:01:10.811 --> 00:01:11.644
- Yeah, it was good.

00:01:11.644 --> 00:01:12.477
- I love a thoughtful gift.

00:01:12.477 --> 00:01:13.320
You grew up in DC, right?

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.153
- I did, yeah.

00:01:14.153 --> 00:01:15.210
- [Kelly] Did you go to the White House?

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.490
- I did as a kid because I
was a childhood friend of

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.833
Amy Carter's in the Carter White House

00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:21.028
- [Kelly] Which is just so random.

00:01:21.028 --> 00:01:24.150
- Yeah, and when you go
like the cam, I mean, again,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.451
even then which was the,
you know, analog '70s,

00:01:26.451 --> 00:01:30.720
it, you know, you would go
like for the weekend, you know,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.774
and you would come back and
like, I have a photograph

00:01:32.774 --> 00:01:36.870
of Amy and President Carter
and myself tobogganing.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.490
And you never saw the photographers,

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.932
would just like show up at the house.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:41.340
So crazy.
- Oh my God.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.543
- Yeah, yeah, crazy.

00:01:42.543 --> 00:01:43.376
- We didn't ...

00:01:43.376 --> 00:01:44.454
- You didn't get to toboggan, huh?

00:01:44.454 --> 00:01:45.287
- We tobogganed, yeah, yeah.

00:01:45.287 --> 00:01:46.260
- You did?
- We did.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.130
It's got these kind of stairs.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.367
- I never got that experience on a ...

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:50.520
- It's a little strange

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.320
'cause it was like a
childhood accident, you know?

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.610
I mean, we were in a program.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:54.990
- [Kelly] I know, that's so cool though.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:55.823
- Yeah.

00:01:55.823 --> 00:01:56.656
- [Kelly] To have that memory.

00:01:56.656 --> 00:01:57.489
- Yeah.

00:01:57.489 --> 00:01:58.804
- Well you, Phil, you play
a soccer star in Ted Lasso.

00:01:58.804 --> 00:02:00.041
- Yes, yeah, I dunno
what I'm doing actually.

00:02:00.041 --> 00:02:00.874
- But you also play,

00:02:00.874 --> 00:02:02.465
you play soccer in real
life though too, right?

00:02:02.465 --> 00:02:03.370
- I do, I do.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.100
- Yeah, have you always loved playing,

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.150
football where you're from?

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.110
- Thank you, yes.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:07.943
(audience laughs)

00:02:07.943 --> 00:02:09.300
- Yes, yes.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.070
Obviously not football
where we're from, but yes,

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:12.329
football where you're from, yes.

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:13.970
- Foot ball.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:14.803
(audience laughs)

00:02:14.803 --> 00:02:16.110
- Here's the thing, here's
the thing, I get it, I know.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.208
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:17.208 --> 00:02:19.380
- Why do they call it a parkway and

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.550
why do they call it a driveway?

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:21.926
I'm just saying like, it's,

00:02:21.926 --> 00:02:24.360
you should call them the
opposite, I'm just saying.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.350
Anyway, so yeah, so yeah.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.060
So you play soccer in real life?

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:27.893
- I do, yes.

00:02:27.893 --> 00:02:32.370
And not at all anywhere
near as well as Jamie does.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.050
I'm a sort of enthusiastic,

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.547
sort of sweaty box-to-box midfielder,

00:02:36.547 --> 00:02:40.860
rather than having any sort
of panache or style with it,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.420
but it's kind of, it,

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.620
since the show has come out,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.810
it's been a sort of double edged sword

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.470
in the sense that I think
there's been a couple of times

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.600
where I've finished a game and

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.710
someone will come up to me afterwards

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.710
and I'm like, sweating, really sweating

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.440
and like really embarrassed
myself a couple of times.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.020
Like miss the ball and
it's gone out, whatever.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:01.875
And now as somebody...

00:03:01.875 --> 00:03:03.286
- And you play a soccer star.

00:03:03.286 --> 00:03:04.617
- Yeah, literally.
(audience laughs)

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.510
- Did they call you out for that?

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:07.343
- [Phil] Sky was like ...

00:03:07.343 --> 00:03:08.370
- "Great job, Jamie."

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.203
- Literally, he was like,

00:03:09.203 --> 00:03:11.268
"Don't you play Jamie Tartt on Ted Lasso?"

00:03:11.268 --> 00:03:12.109
(all laugh)

00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:14.137
I'm like, "Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah."

00:03:14.137 --> 00:03:15.370
- [Kelly] "I'm just having an off day."

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:16.203
- Yeah.

00:03:16.203 --> 00:03:18.270
But they have really great
editors that make us look

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.260
like we know what we're doing.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.210
And it's, it's just like, it's a really,

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.560
like it's like a dance really.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.940
It's like choreography more than it is

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.190
actually playing football
because you've gotta, you know,

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.410
you've gotta hit, you know,

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.600
you've gotta hit your
mark as you would normally

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.433
when you're acting.

00:03:31.433 --> 00:03:32.266
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:32.266 --> 00:03:33.099
- That sounds so stressful.

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:33.960
- It's stressful, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:34.993
- It's just working out to us.

00:03:34.993 --> 00:03:37.393
- [Ana] Yeah.
(all laugh)

00:03:37.393 --> 00:03:39.240
- I love that you pointed
out though, editors,

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.240
like editors never get
the credit they deserve

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.940
because they make you look so good.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:45.745
(everyone claps)

00:03:45.745 --> 00:03:47.043
Like in, I just got into TV world.

00:03:47.043 --> 00:03:47.876
- Yeah.

00:03:47.876 --> 00:03:49.590
- Like, I mean, I obviously
started in TV world

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.790
but I didn't really get it until now.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.740
And like, on "The Voice",
whether it's this show

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.290
or anything you see, it's just
like the editors really are

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.918
the magic makers I feel
like, they're so key.

00:03:57.918 --> 00:04:01.620
Is it true that you're also
a video game character now?

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:02.670
I mean, I think you've made it

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:03.828
when you're a video game game character.

00:04:03.828 --> 00:04:04.770
- Yeah.
- You've arrived.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:06.260
- I'm just saying.
(audience applauds)

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.150
- This is my last public
appearance, this is it.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:08.983
(audience applauds)

00:04:08.983 --> 00:04:09.990
- This is my real question.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:13.140
And you have to be,
(audience cheers)

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.330
you have to be honest.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:18.390
Have you ever played yourself in the game?

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.942
Like you're ...
- Yes.

00:04:19.942 --> 00:04:22.049
- Okay!
I was like...

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:22.908
(audience applauds)

00:04:22.908 --> 00:04:26.280
"Guy, I would play me."

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.086
I'd be like, "I'm killing it."

00:04:28.086 --> 00:04:30.270
- He's also really good as well,

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.974
so he's like, he's,

00:04:31.974 --> 00:04:34.156
I just give the ball to him all the time.

00:04:34.156 --> 00:04:35.516
(audience laughs)

00:04:35.516 --> 00:04:36.349
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:36.349 --> 00:04:38.662
- There was a time when my
girlfriend came back home,

00:04:38.662 --> 00:04:41.233
and I mean, it puts a whole
different meaning to her

00:04:41.233 --> 00:04:46.233
finding you playing with
yourself but it's with myself.

00:04:46.366 --> 00:04:48.150
(all laugh)

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.453
And she came ...

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.010
- So your girlfriend came in.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:58.574
- She was like, "Not again."
(all laugh)

00:04:58.574 --> 00:05:00.620
Yeah, it's, rather embarrassing.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:03.462
- Oh my, it's nothing worse
than that bust, I mean.

00:05:03.462 --> 00:05:06.545
(all laugh and clap)

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.305
- [Kelly] I love this man though.

00:05:11.305 --> 00:05:12.138
- Nothing worse.

00:05:12.138 --> 00:05:14.400
I mean, my children have
caught me watching old sketches

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.450
of mine howling and laughing
at myself, nothing ...

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.283
- The good old, the good days.

00:05:19.283 --> 00:05:20.116
- [Ana] It's humiliating.

00:05:20.116 --> 00:05:21.270
- Oh my God, it's awesome.

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:24.038
- I still watch it, but
I'm like, "Start it over."

00:05:24.038 --> 00:05:26.440
- "No wait, you missed this part."

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:27.273
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:27.273 --> 00:05:28.920
"Look, come watch this,
this is the best bit."

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.320
Yeah.
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

